<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>About AuthArena</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css">
</head>

<body>

    <%- include("partials/navbar") %>

    <section class="about-hero">

        <div class="hero-overlay"></div>

        <div class="hero-content">

            <h1>
                Welcome to AuthArena
            </h1>

            <p>
                A complete beginner friendly authentication playground to learn,
                build, and experiment with real backend authentication systems.
            </p>

            <a href="/">
                <button>
                    Explore Auth Systems
                </button>
            </a>

        </div>

    </section>

    <section class="about-container">

        <div class="about-card">

            <h2>
                Learn By Building
            </h2>

            <p>
                AuthArena focuses on practical backend learning through real
                authentication implementations instead of only theoretical
                explanations.
            </p>

            <p>
                Every module is separated cleanly so you can understand how
                different authentication systems actually work in production
                style applications.
            </p>

        </div>

        <div class="about-card">

            <h2>
                Authentication Systems Included
            </h2>

            <ul>

                <li>
                    JWT Authentication
                </li>

                <li>
                    Refresh Token Flow
                </li>

                <li>
                    Session Based Authentication
                </li>

                <li>
                    Google OAuth Authentication
                </li>

                <li>
                    OTP Verification
                </li>

                <li>
                    Role Based Access Control
                </li>

                <li>
                    MFA / 2FA Systems
                </li>

            </ul>

        </div>

        <div class="about-card">

            <h2>
                Beginner Friendly Architecture
            </h2>

            <p>
                This project is intentionally designed with simple folder
                structures, readable code, and isolated modules to help
                beginners learn backend authentication faster.
            </p>

            <p>
                You can easily inspect middleware, cookies, sessions,
                access tokens, refresh tokens, and route protection.
            </p>

        </div>

        <div class="about-card">

            <h2>
                Flexible Database Choices
            </h2>

            <p>
                The current implementation uses in-memory arrays for simplicity
                and easier learning.
            </p>

            <p>
                Later you can upgrade the exact same systems using:
            </p>

            <ul>

                <li>
                    LowDB
                </li>

                <li>
                    MongoDB
                </li>

                <li>
                    PostgreSQL
                </li>

                <li>
                    Redis Sessions
                </li>

            </ul>

        </div>

        <div class="about-card">

            <h2>
                Built For Real Developers
            </h2>

            <p>
                AuthArena is inspired by real problems developers face while
                implementing authentication systems in actual applications.
            </p>

            <p>
                The goal is not just learning syntax, but understanding complete
                authentication flows and backend thinking.
            </p>

        </div>

        <div class="about-card">

            <h2>
                Your Backend Playground
            </h2>

            <p>
                Experiment freely with authentication flows, route protection,
                cookies, OAuth redirects, sessions, and security concepts
                inside one unified application.
            </p>

            <p>
                Perfect for beginners preparing for backend development,
                internships, and full stack projects.
            </p>

        </div>

    </section>

    <%- include("partials/footer") %>

</body>
</html>